.TITLE "wsl"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Windows Subsystem for Linux allows developers to run a GNU/Linux environment directly on Windows. It provides a seamless experience for running __command line tools__ and __applications__ without the overhead of a traditional virtual machine.

.DIV "TLDR"
**wsl**
__Starts__ the default Linux distribution in the current terminal.
> 

**wsl --install**
__Installs__ the default Ubuntu distribution and the necessary __subsystem components__.
> __--install__ install flag

**wsl --list --online**
__Displays__ a list of all available Linux __distributions__ that can be installed.
> __--list__ list flag | __--online__ remote source flag

**wsl --distribution name**
__Runs__ a specific Linux __distribution__ by its name.
> __--distribution__ distribution flag | __name__ the name of the distro

**wsl --update**
__Checks__ for and __installs__ updates to the WSL kernel.
> __--update__ update flag

**wsl --shutdown**
__Terminates__ all running distributions and the WSL 2 __lightweight utility VM__.
> __--shutdown__ power off flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Always use __wsl --shutdown__ if you notice high memory usage from the Vmmem process. For the best performance and compatibility, ensure you are using __WSL 2__ instead of the legacy version 1.

